  "regressions": 3,
  "scope": "Whole Federer 3.2.36, pp. 272--273: actual compact-convex volume, joint projected-volume and intrinsic-volume continuity; full actual Cartesian intrinsic-volume convolution on arbitrary original nonempty bounded convex factors; actual finite elementary symmetric edge coefficients for every rectangular box; intrinsic-volume invariance on arbitrary original bounded convex sources and Q_1 invariance on every source subset under arbitrary metric isometric injections. Retain all natural admissible degrees and ambient blocks, zero widths, lower-dimensional and non-Borel convex sources, positive degree-zero atoms and infinite Q_1 values.",
  "proof_route": "Actual Steiner tube bounds and exact compact projection-image laws give all three continuities. Actual squared product distance, whole first-distance fibres, the full rectifiable product theorem, zero-slice rectangle mass and distance coarea give the whole product tube formula. The existing actual ball-section profile and polar formula evaluate every radial coefficient; scalar singleton nullity removes the nonzero zero-section endpoint. Finite nonnegative integration and the internal positive-radius root count give the normalized original-set convolution. Independently specified elementary symmetric coefficient laws, actual interval bases, coordinate carrier products and actual frame isometries prove every box value. Polarization proves arbitrary isometric maps affine; local common-ambient orthogonal extensions, actual tube-volume invariance and point convolutions give intrinsic-volume invariance. Original all-set closure laws restore bounded convex sources. Both actual finite-cutoff closed-convex generator transports prove Q_1 invariance, with empty preimages contributing zero.",
  "whole_original_convex_source": true,
  "no_source_measurability_premise": true,
